# Differential test of refinements.js: values a typeof or truthiness branch
# narrowed lower to ctnative.refine, spelled as the operand or as
# ctnative::as_string / ctnative::as_number. The C++ is compiled against
# public Core, checked for interpreter symbols with nm, run, and every global
# compared with the interpreter's (compilation-unit.py). The negative
# changes the global `o1` and requires the comparison to fail naming it.
# compile-clean.py checks a warning-free build on both toolchains.
# string-arrays-calls.py is the generic pipeline driver for a fixture that is
# not registered in NativeFixtures.cmake.

# RUN: python3 %S/string-arrays-calls.py --translate ctjs-translate --opt ctjs-opt --js %S/refinements.js --out %t/refinements.emitc.mlir
# RUN: ctjs-translate --mlir-to-cpp %t/refinements.emitc.mlir | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %compilation_unit --module %t/refinements.emitc.mlir --js %S/refinements.js --work %t --name refinements --core-build %build
# RUN: not %compilation_unit --module %t/refinements.emitc.mlir --js %S/refinements.js --work %t --name refinements_negative --core-build %build --mutate o1 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NEGATIVE
# RUN: %compile_clean --module %t/refinements.emitc.mlir --work %t --name refinements

# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::as_string(
# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::as_number(
# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::Number.parseInt(
# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::Number.parseFloat(
# NEGATIVE: global 'o1' differs
